1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,892
There is a book the New
Testament quotes by name, and

2
00:00:03,892 --> 00:00:06,481
most Bibles in the world
do not contain it.

3
00:00:06,931 --> 00:00:10,257
Its oldest pieces were found
in caves by the Dead Sea,

4
00:00:10,257 --> 00:00:13,459
written in Aramaic more than
two thousand years ago.

5
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:16,960
But the only complete
copy on earth survived

6
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,456
in one language: Ge'ez. In Ethiopia.

7
00:00:19,906 --> 00:00:22,890
It is the Book of Enoch.
And it begins with angels

8
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:25,517
who bound themselves
with an oath, and fell.

9
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:29,636
So pour a cup. Tonight we open
the chapters of the Watchers.

10
00:00:31,586 --> 00:00:34,402
First, as always: what
kind of story is this?

11
00:00:34,852 --> 00:00:38,737
This is scripture. The Book of
Enoch, Henok, is one of the

12
00:00:38,737 --> 00:00:42,020
eighty‑one books of our
Ethiopian Orthodox Bible.

13
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:46,944
Tonight's chapters are First
Enoch, six to eleven, in

14
00:00:46,944 --> 00:00:50,321
the English of R. H. Charles, from 1917.

15
00:00:50,771 --> 00:00:53,961
Scholars debate when these
chapters were written. Many

16
00:00:53,961 --> 00:00:56,915
place them around the third
century before Christ.

17
00:00:57,365 --> 00:01:00,131
We'll tell you plainly
what the text says, what

18
00:01:00,131 --> 00:01:02,485
scholars propose, and what nobody knows.

19
00:01:04,435 --> 00:01:09,512
The first cup is Abol, the strongest. And
our story begins with a strong desire.

20
00:01:11,462 --> 00:01:14,070
In the days when people
multiplied on the earth,

21
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:16,134
beautiful daughters were born to them.

22
00:01:16,584 --> 00:01:19,353
The Book of Enoch says
the angels, the children

23
00:01:19,353 --> 00:01:21,533
of heaven, saw them and desired them.

24
00:01:21,983 --> 00:01:25,448
They said to one another: "Come,
let us choose us wives from

25
00:01:25,448 --> 00:01:28,277
among the children of men
and beget us children."

26
00:01:28,727 --> 00:01:32,183
Their leader, Semyaza, was
afraid. He feared that he

27
00:01:32,183 --> 00:01:35,041
alone would pay the
penalty of a great sin.

28
00:01:35,491 --> 00:01:37,975
So they all swore an oath,
and bound themselves

29
00:01:37,975 --> 00:01:40,035
together, so that none could turn back.

30
00:01:40,485 --> 00:01:42,825
There were two hundred
of them, and they came

31
00:01:42,825 --> 00:01:44,645
down on the summit of Mount Hermon.

32
00:01:45,095 --> 00:01:48,797
The text says they named it
Hermon because they had sworn and

33
00:01:48,797 --> 00:01:52,135
bound themselves upon it. A
mountain named for an oath.

34
00:01:54,085 --> 00:01:57,861
They took wives. And they taught
people what heaven had not given them.

35
00:01:58,311 --> 00:02:01,761
The text names charms and
enchantments, and the cutting

36
00:02:01,761 --> 00:02:04,583
of roots. It only names
them, and so will we.

37
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:08,152
Their children were giants,
who devoured the labour of

38
00:02:08,152 --> 00:02:10,751
people, and then turned
on people themselves.

39
00:02:11,201 --> 00:02:14,534
Azazel taught the making of
swords and armour, bracelets

40
00:02:14,534 --> 00:02:17,153
and ornaments, and the
colouring of eyelids.

41
00:02:17,603 --> 00:02:21,028
Godlessness spread. And
Charles translates: "Then the

42
00:02:21,028 --> 00:02:24,131
earth laid accusation
against the lawless ones."

43
00:02:24,581 --> 00:02:27,933
So here is the question for
the first cup: what happens

44
00:02:27,933 --> 00:02:30,981
when even angels choose
their own will over God's?

45
00:02:32,931 --> 00:02:35,533
Did you know? Azazel
once had another name.

46
00:02:35,983 --> 00:02:40,729
In the oldest Aramaic list of the
Watchers' chiefs, the tenth name is

47
00:02:40,729 --> 00:02:45,199
Asael. Over centuries, copyists'
spellings drifted toward Azazel.

48
00:02:45,649 --> 00:02:49,145
Even in Charles's English,
the same figure is Asael

49
00:02:49,145 --> 00:02:52,092
in chapter six and
Azazel in chapter eight.

50
00:02:52,542 --> 00:02:56,452
Names change as stories are
copied. Like Kaldi in the coffee

51
00:02:56,452 --> 00:02:59,710
legend, it pays to ask
where a name first appears.

52
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:06,268
The second cup is Tona. The talk turns,
and the story turns toward heaven.

53
00:03:08,218 --> 00:03:10,597
As people perished, the text says, "they

54
00:03:10,597 --> 00:03:12,975
cried, and their cry went up to heaven."

55
00:03:13,425 --> 00:03:18,673
Four great archangels looked down:
Michael, Uriel, Raphael and Gabriel.

56
00:03:19,123 --> 00:03:21,589
They saw the blood shed
upon the earth, and they

57
00:03:21,589 --> 00:03:24,158
brought the cry of the
earth before the Most High.

58
00:03:24,608 --> 00:03:28,789
And God answered. Not with silence,
but with judgment and with mercy.

59
00:03:30,739 --> 00:03:35,582
First, mercy for one man. An angel
is sent to the son of Lamech: Noah.

60
00:03:36,032 --> 00:03:38,877
Tell him in my name, "Hide
thyself!" A flood is

61
00:03:38,877 --> 00:03:41,237
coming, but his seed will be preserved.

62
00:03:41,687 --> 00:03:44,843
Then the Lord said to
Raphael: bind Azazel hand

63
00:03:44,843 --> 00:03:47,597
and foot, and cast him into the darkness.

64
00:03:48,047 --> 00:03:51,429
"The whole earth has been
corrupted through the works that

65
00:03:51,429 --> 00:03:54,169
were taught by Azazel:
to him ascribe all sin."

66
00:03:54,619 --> 00:03:57,145
Michael is sent to bind Semyaza and his

67
00:03:57,145 --> 00:03:59,995
companions, until the
day of their judgment.

68
00:04:00,445 --> 00:04:03,995
So here is the question for
the second cup: why does the

69
00:04:03,995 --> 00:04:07,037
healing of the world begin
by saving one family?

70
00:04:08,987 --> 00:04:11,249
Did you know how this
book came down to us?

71
00:04:11,699 --> 00:04:16,428
The oldest pieces are Aramaic fragments
from Cave Four at Qumran. The

72
00:04:16,428 --> 00:04:20,403
oldest is dated to around two
hundred years before Christ.

73
00:04:20,853 --> 00:04:24,587
Greek pieces survived too.
Chapters one to thirty‑two were

74
00:04:24,587 --> 00:04:27,935
found at Akhmim, in Egypt,
in the eighteen‑eighties.

75
00:04:28,385 --> 00:04:31,646
But the whole book, beginning
to end, survived only in

76
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,785
Ge'ez, because our Church
kept it as holy scripture.

77
00:04:35,235 --> 00:04:41,417
In 1773 the traveller James Bruce
carried Ethiopian copies to

78
00:04:41,417 --> 00:04:46,990
Europe. The first English
translation followed in 1821.

79
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:52,131
For two centuries, books said
Bruce brought three copies. A 2023

80
00:04:52,131 --> 00:04:56,016
study counts four: in Paris,
Britain and the Vatican.

81
00:04:56,466 --> 00:04:59,410
Even the history of the history
is still being checked.

82
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:06,117
The third cup is Bereka, the blessing.
And this story, too, ends in blessing.

83
00:05:08,067 --> 00:05:12,590
After the judgment, the Lord says:
"cleanse thou the earth from all
oppression."

84
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:15,365
The store chambers of blessing are opened.

85
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:19,128
And the text promises: "truth
and peace shall be associated

86
00:05:19,128 --> 00:05:21,767
together throughout all
the days of the world."

87
00:05:22,217 --> 00:05:25,468
Pride bound itself with an
oath, and fell. But God's

88
00:05:25,468 --> 00:05:28,468
promise is peace, and His
promise does not fail.

89
00:05:30,418 --> 00:05:34,109
And one more blessing, for anyone
who has wondered about this book.

90
00:05:34,559 --> 00:05:38,185
The Letter of Jude, found in
every Christian Bible, quotes it.

91
00:05:38,635 --> 00:05:42,930
"And Enoch also, the seventh from
Adam, prophesied of these, saying,

92
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:46,593
Behold, the Lord cometh with
ten thousands of his saints."

93
00:05:47,043 --> 00:05:50,648
Around the year two hundred,
the Christian writer Tertullian

94
00:05:50,648 --> 00:05:53,592
pointed to that verse in
defence of Enoch's book.

95
00:05:54,042 --> 00:05:56,909
Genesis remembers these
days in one short verse:

96
00:05:56,909 --> 00:05:59,717
"There were giants in the
earth in those days."

97
00:06:00,167 --> 00:06:03,623
Enoch tells the longer story.
And our Church kept it whole.

98
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:07,429
So what do the Watchers teach us?

99
00:06:07,879 --> 00:06:11,037
They wanted what was not
given to them, and swore

100
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:14,001
never to turn back.
Self‑will, bound by pride.

101
00:06:14,451 --> 00:06:17,614
And notice how this book
is talked about online.

102
00:06:17,614 --> 00:06:20,382
Videos call it banned, or lost, or secret.

103
00:06:20,832 --> 00:06:25,078
It was never lost. Our Church has
kept and copied it for centuries, and

104
00:06:25,078 --> 00:06:28,725
scholars can show you the
fragments, the Greek and the Ge'ez.

105
00:06:29,175 --> 00:06:33,419
So before you believe a viral
claim about giants or angels, look

106
00:06:33,419 --> 00:06:37,133
it up. Read the chapter itself.
Ask where it comes from.

107
00:06:39,083 --> 00:06:42,902
Stories of fallen angels can
pull us toward fear, or toward

108
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:46,592
endless theories and doom‑scrolling.
Neither is the path.

109
00:06:47,042 --> 00:06:51,161
The Watchers fell through pride
and self‑will. The Christian way

110
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:54,573
is humble obedience, quiet
prayer, and patient trust.

111
00:06:55,023 --> 00:06:58,338
Tonight, read a few verses
slowly, and ask God for a

112
00:06:58,338 --> 00:07:00,825
humble heart. That is enough for today.

113
00:07:02,775 --> 00:07:06,551
The Book of Enoch is long, and
tonight we only opened its door.

114
00:07:07,001 --> 00:07:10,799
Tell us below: has anyone in your
family read the Book of Enoch?

115
00:07:11,249 --> 00:07:14,811
Until then, stay for the
third cup. This is Ethiopics.
